                "entry_id": "57050c87-ab9c-3e2d-9bbc-740f24be74e2",
                "word": "unspecified",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3225cae2-307e-3b36-9873-77b3899b7d19",
                        "entry_id": "57050c87-ab9c-3e2d-9bbc-740f24be74e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not specified; not thoroughly explained or detailed; not adequately commented."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d0b758c-3605-4999-9b29-aba04151ff0c",
                                "sense_id": "3225cae2-307e-3b36-9873-77b3899b7d19",
                                "text": "Ranicide in rats was found to be reduced by injection of noradrenaline into the hypothalamus, as was muricide behaviour (Bandler, 1970).[…]Other sites in the unspecified ‘ventral midbrain’ were also found (Bandler, 1971) at which noradrenaline administration in crystalline form served to facilitate predatory aggression (ranicide and muricide)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b51d061-e142-441d-8f16-4a1b0f63a9f7",
                                "sense_id": "3225cae2-307e-3b36-9873-77b3899b7d19",
                                "text": "Obviously, we must reject the existence of an unqualified or unspecified right to know. If the right to know did not require disclosure of only specific (types of) data or information, a person could be said to have a right to know just anything whatsoever."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "833820c5-c2ff-4f62-828e-40510d2b3c6e",
                                "sense_id": "3225cae2-307e-3b36-9873-77b3899b7d19",
                                "text": "Howard Gleckman of the Tax Policy Center calls these unspecified sources of revenue “mystery meat,” and strongly suggests that nothing like this would actually happen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
